 # TIP-Editor
 
+Also called: Text and Image Prompt-based Editor for 3D Gaussian Splatting
 
 ## Overview
-TIP-Editor is a method for editing existing 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) scenes using intuitive text and image prompts [S1]. It solves the problem of local, high-fidelity modification by combining a stepwise 2D personalization strategy with score distillation sampling (SDS) [S1]. It is distinguished from sibling methods by its specific integration of LoRA for reference image alignment and a dedicated localization loss for scene adaptation, rather than relying solely on attention maps or ControlNet depth conditioning [S1].
+TIP-Editor is a method for editing existing 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) scenes using intuitive text and image prompts [S1]. It solves the problem of achieving accurate local editing while maintaining multi-view consistency, which is often compromised in text-guided 3D editing [S1]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [GaussCtrl](14877-gaussctrl.md) by employing a stepwise 2D personalization strategy with LoRA-based reference image alignment and localization loss, rather than relying on depth-conditioned ControlNet for geometric consistency [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** An existing 3DGS scene (set of Gaussians), text prompts, and reference images for content personalization.
-**Outputs:** Edited 3DGS scene.
